---
import Figure from '../Figure.astro';
---

<Figure
  kind="Diagram"
  title="What sits between your devices and the ISP"
  caption="The access line enters at the modem (or the ONT on fibre), which only converts signals. The box sold as a home router holds several devices: the router itself with NAT and a firewall, DHCP and DNS services, a switch for the wired ports, and a Wi-Fi access point that bridges wireless devices onto the same LAN. To every device inside, the router is the default gateway."
>
  <svg class="hn-svg" viewBox="0 0 440 300" role="img" aria-label="Home network: ISP line, modem, home router with its parts, and devices">
    <defs>
      <marker id="hn-arr" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" fill="var(--text-muted)"></path></marker>
    </defs>
    <line class="hn-wire" x1="40" y1="45" x2="40" y2="78" marker-end="url(#hn-arr)"></line>
    <text class="hn-lbl" x="52" y="30" text-anchor="start">ISP access line: coax, phone copper, fibre or 4G/5G</text>
    <rect class="hn-dev" x="10" y="80" width="80" height="44" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="hn-t" x="50" y="96">modem</text>
    <text class="hn-s" x="50" y="112">or ONT</text>
    <line class="hn-wire" x1="90" y1="102" x2="128" y2="102" marker-end="url(#hn-arr)"></line>
    <text class="hn-s" x="110" y="90">WAN</text>

    <rect class="hn-box" x="130" y="50" width="300" height="160" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="hn-box-t" x="280" y="66">"home router" box</text>
    <rect class="hn-part hn-gw" x="145" y="80" width="130" height="50" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="hn-t" x="210" y="98">router</text>
    <text class="hn-s" x="210" y="116">NAT · firewall</text>
    <rect class="hn-part" x="290" y="80" width="125" height="50" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="hn-t" x="352" y="98">services</text>
    <text class="hn-s" x="352" y="116">DHCP · DNS</text>
    <rect class="hn-part" x="145" y="148" width="130" height="46" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="hn-t" x="210" y="164">switch</text>
    <text class="hn-s" x="210" y="180">LAN ports</text>
    <rect class="hn-part" x="290" y="148" width="125" height="46" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="hn-t" x="352" y="164">Wi-Fi AP</text>
    <text class="hn-s" x="352" y="180">bridge to LAN</text>
    <line class="hn-wire" x1="210" y1="130" x2="210" y2="148"></line>
    <line class="hn-wire" x1="275" y1="171" x2="290" y2="171"></line>
    <line class="hn-wire" x1="275" y1="105" x2="290" y2="105"></line>

    <line class="hn-wire" x1="180" y1="194" x2="180" y2="240"></line>
    <line class="hn-wire" x1="240" y1="194" x2="240" y2="240"></line>
    <rect class="hn-end" x="150" y="240" width="60" height="30" rx="5"></rect>
    <text class="hn-t" x="180" y="255">PC</text>
    <rect class="hn-end" x="212" y="240" width="56" height="30" rx="5"></rect>
    <text class="hn-t" x="240" y="255">TV</text>
    <path class="hn-radio" d="M330 200 q10 10 0 20 M340 198 q14 14 0 28"></path>
    <rect class="hn-end" x="300" y="240" width="58" height="30" rx="5"></rect>
    <text class="hn-t" x="329" y="255">phone</text>
    <rect class="hn-end" x="364" y="240" width="62" height="30" rx="5"></rect>
    <text class="hn-t" x="395" y="255">laptop</text>
    <text class="hn-lbl" x="280" y="290">devices: 192.168.1.x, default gateway 192.168.1.1</text>
  </svg>
</Figure>

<style>
  .hn-svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 440px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .hn-wire {
    stroke: var(--text-muted);
    stroke-width: 1.6;
  }
  .hn-radio {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--g-blue);
    stroke-width: 1.6;
  }
  .hn-dev {
    fill: rgba(251, 188, 5, 0.16);
    stroke: var(--g-yellow);
  }
  .hn-box {
    fill: transparent;
    stroke: var(--border-strong);
    stroke-dasharray: 6 4;
  }
  .hn-part {
    fill: rgba(66, 133, 244, 0.16);
    stroke: var(--g-blue);
  }
  .hn-gw {
    fill: rgba(52, 168, 83, 0.18);
    stroke: var(--g-green);
  }
  .hn-end {
    fill: transparent;
    stroke: var(--border-strong);
  }
  .hn-t {
    fill: var(--text);
    font: 12px var(--font-mono);
    text-anchor: middle;
    dominant-baseline: central;
  }
  .hn-s {
    fill: var(--text-muted);
    font: 10px var(--font-mono);
    text-anchor: middle;
    dominant-baseline: central;
  }
  .hn-lbl {
    fill: var(--text-muted);
    font: 10px var(--font-mono);
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
  .hn-box-t {
    fill: var(--text-muted);
    font: 10px var(--font-mono);
    text-anchor: middle;
    dominant-baseline: central;
  }
</style>
